{
 "_readme": [
  "ROLE SETS for the Meshy clip pipeline (tools/meshy_clip_library.py).",
  "",
  "WHY SETS EXIST: Meshy's exporter can only carry the LAST 20 ACTIONS selected on a",
  "model, so 20 is a HARD architectural cap per baked variant -- not a preference.",
  "The agreed rule is VARIANTS BY ROLE, MERGE BY CHARACTER-WHO-NEEDS-BOTH: bake each",
  "role as its own <=20-clip variant, then fuse whatever a given character actually",
  "needs into one GLB locally with tools/glb-merge-anims.mjs, which is FREE and has",
  "no 20-clip limit.",
  "",
  "Entries are ['<meshy_action_name>', '<engine_clip_name>']. The Meshy name is",
  "resolved to its integer action_id against tools/meshy_actions.json at runtime, so",
  "ids are never hand-typed here. The engine name is what the merged GLB's",
  "AnimationGroup gets called.",
  "",
  "LOCOMOTION USES _inplace WHEREVER MESHY SHIPS ONE. Meshy publishes ~90 clips",
  "twice: root-motion original and an `_inplace` twin with root translation stripped.",
  "Engine-driven movement (character controller / navmesh / RTS steering) wants the",
  "_inplace twin, otherwise the mesh slides out of its collision capsule.",
  "",
  "COST: every clip costs 3 credits to bake. per_set_credits = clips x 3. Rigging a",
  "character costs 5 credits ONCE; every set baked onto that same rig_task_id reuses",
  "it for free."
 ],
 "credits_per_clip": 3,
 "credits_per_rig": 5,
 "export_cap": 20,

